{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0b432d9882c48a5c04da761fb14d60eee5ba9d69876cf91c4d9476cd9724309f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_333cc1db0b84ca315c6fe9ebc127b79df301ce8702110eaf156842478494d1bf"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Séance is a GTK4 terminal multiplexer for Linux that auto-detects Claude Code, Codex, Pi, OpenCode, and Antigravity CLI sessions running inside it and tracks their status live in a sidebar.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_142cece552d1144c16f1fcbfbdbf52c20b6292bf20a9c78a9a042f2ddd574db9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_49450ead78ade87fae4c4e9b11109859493321711dca0942ee4505c83f0a27ea","slc_672b9049bb8459bc57dbc0105d73385ddc2f78c2ffdbc923f74e2c3525db6e26","slc_d26e56273445082d2e3c7a05f194e0f30190a1520c5720493027717982557c89"],"source_ids":["src_3fdeda5ae7f852f9bab7f1243d72c67f"],"text":"Repository development practice: security issues must be reported privately via GitHub's private vulnerability reporting rather than public issues, with acknowledgment aimed within 72 hours; only the latest pre-1.0 release is supported with security fixes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_27e25a6d258d5404d5927eade9e5fa7cb9bed22f2c8586a636f2c75d07b756c3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_56d2a2f3b9f1a0cb46519eea12d7fbeb700a88533ba4b7f1f53c65e000365de1"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Panes are arranged in a horizontally scrolling strip, a layout model borrowed from niri, described as fitting long linear agent sessions better than a tiling grid.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3c3752a63ed9393219506eed404d3fc8949dec80ea99af47b476b12b04d8edd7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15ddd20c23c73dada11b32bfd7b3511dfd200b6d3660ac20a78c971e485c0daa","slc_6ecae7f6977169d538fb2c21ba880a6e5bb92b10dad077e26b76f17805f0805b"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Terminal rendering is GPU-accelerated via libghostty (Ghostty used as a library), and the app is built with Zig, GTK4, and libadwaita.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4c9ff3aee28a9357e53c014246fb19988679dfe1317be7855c5d9c35b52db31b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21c357ed76f4b72c9bad2f4bffe9b27c9f7829afaace43e033c1c37219ab41e1"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Remote `opencode attach` sessions and `--pure` OpenCode launches are not tracked.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_68d285b24c93ee4585c1ea420859df5bd63b8e22b6ca6ad58644bb26ca2fc7ad","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2ae792e5dad4976af9c47954595d05749f3e1365139e80f8d7646f0abe0df316"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Antigravity CLI tracking uses its status-line callback, which the wrapper adds to ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json on first launch, keeping a backup at settings.json.seance-backup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_803cd32fad2502b6317608c3b2717bfc976202452825fb6fb903bd1a7ab8c9d1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a450d6aad2e331ea41cf75e4e03179409b0117a6d4ee7989bde37652c9e902b","slc_d913b998354bc0c423346cb9eb8c63d9f56abf63ed4527eb205443c9bc8f688a"],"source_ids":["src_c824506cb3725ff68812c3dfa5e1b8ed"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run `G_DEBUG=fatal-criticals GTK_A11Y=none xvfb-run -a zig build test` and `xvfb-run zig build e2e`, and CI must pass before merge.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d9f6096a4449c892b9d9f7ab6c43e95fe78152eaa39f8bfdb4698a739a1bb893","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f4701464d624cde74bb3b74e8525ed1b9b8b2427d4fe655024977cab3179c32d"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"The product includes workspaces, session persistence across restarts, tabs within columns, a command palette, focus-follows-mouse, and no telemetry; F11 toggles fullscreen and the header bar hides in fullscreen.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_edd8647667664411b743c2f02e1f5ed4ca3b6a8c1aef1bed7faa31699fbe158e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"no1msd/seance@f3b74415085d snapshot 88cf718b6e2c2927","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d9e6a8a8b867bb20936a8ee0b7b6685d988d9bda0042898a43a9bbb7ab44bbf1"],"source_ids":["src_70dc1db2c3785338b20263c990e638bc"],"text":"Every action is available through `seance ctl`, which talks to the running instance over a Unix domain socket; scripts can create workspaces, open panes, send input, read terminal output, and query the session hierarchy, with JSON output for all commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:10:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0d5ca2e20fac4657b8d4e45ab024490b"}
